// Paginates the document from paragraph lgfrom on and answers how many paragraphs it walked: pages are filled with paragraphs in order, a paragraph is split between pages at a line, and a paragraph that asks for a break starts a page. Every paragraph must have been laid out (lay_all or lay_relayout). starts then holds the start of every page, and one more entry (the paragraph count, line 0) that ends the last; tops holds each paragraph's top in the continuous document. The walk resumes at the page before lgfrom and never stops early, so lgfrom only says where the document may be left as it was; lay_relayout is the one that stops when a page start matches (lay_walk).
lay_paginate(View lgv, int lgfrom) {
  int lgn = lay_walk(lgv, lgfrom, len(lgv.doc.body.paras));
} return int lgn;
